Sigil Linux examples (docs/LINUX.md in the Sigil repository)

  hello.c        the classic, built with the board's gcc
  malloc_test.c  glibc malloc/realloc/free, small (brk) and large (mmap)
  numa_hbm.c     DDR4 (node 0) vs HBM (node 1) with libnuma: placement
                 check and a write / dependent-load timing per node
  rvv_vadd.c     user-space vector (Zve64d, VLEN 512) with RVV intrinsics

  make && make run
  numactl --hardware             # the two memory nodes
  numactl --membind=1 ./prog     # run any program with its memory in HBM
